 ## Runtime ownership and retained boundaries
 
-Most `app/*Page.tsx` adapters create a root with `createRoot` and synchronously commit typed page props. Practice/Sequence parents and their Run/Review children use shared retained-subtree/contents adapters. [RetainedNode](../../packages/ui/src/RetainedNode/RetainedNode.tsx) preserves exact platform-owned subtrees; [retainedPage.tsx](../../apps/web/src/app/retainedPage.tsx) handles parent transfer and recovery. [modulePreparation.js](../../src/modulePreparation.js) caches imports without mounting a page. Loading is not permission to replace active forms or capture state. Two static catalogs use build-produced, inert HTML template fragments from their same typed source. src/staticCatalog.js materializes Practice choices during its normal startup handler and calibration choices before the first Learn render. The helper moves already-parsed template nodes, preserving the host/delegated handlers and exact card DOM without runtime HTML-string parsing or connecting hidden calibration controls during initial startup. No stored/user HTML enters that path; the build helper permits only these catalog roots and rejects nested scripts.
+Most `app/*Page.tsx` adapters create a root with `createRoot` and synchronously commit typed page props. Practice/Sequence parents and their Run/Review children use shared retained-subtree/contents adapters. [RetainedNode](../../packages/ui/src/RetainedNode/RetainedNode.tsx) preserves exact platform-owned subtrees; [retainedPage.tsx](../../apps/web/src/app/retainedPage.tsx) handles parent transfer and recovery. [modulePreparation.js](../../src/modulePreparation.js) caches imports without mounting a page. Loading is not permission to replace active forms or capture state. Two static catalogs retain build-produced escaped HTML as non-executable text until their page opens. src/staticCatalog.js parses only that trusted typed output into a temporary template before first Drills/Learn display, preserving the host, delegated handlers and exact card DOM. Hidden catalog controls are not parsed during initial startup. No stored/user HTML enters that path; the build helper permits only the two known catalog roots and rejects nested scripts.
 
 Startup adapters are deliberate: they serve immediate data, controls and failed/offline loads before React takes ownership. Guarded updates select one current owner. Mount failure restores prior nodes/listeners/focus. Keep native invalid-number drafts, file input, meter and preview controls intact. Practice/Sequence engine differences and save-retry semantics remain separate even when their presentation is shared. Full History graphs load only when needed, and cannot block saved text or repaint a different gun/route.
 
